TA-backup
====

Collects backup-system health: last snapshot age and count for restic and borg repositories (from a config file), and active backup-related systemd timers (restic/borg/b2/rclone/duplicity/timeshift units). Emits JSON events to index=main (sourcetype backup:status) and backup.* metrics to index=metrics (sourcetype backup:metrics) - configured flag, snapshot counts, snapshot age in hours, active timer count - with dashboards.

Prerequisites
-------------
  * Optional: a repo config at local/backup.conf (restic_repository=borg_repository=...) and the restic/borg CLI + passwords; absent hosts report 'not-configured'
  * systemd timers are used for cadence signals; systemd required
  * Splunk Enterprise or Universal Forwarder 9.x - 10.6 (forwarder recommended
    on monitored hosts).
  * A metrics-typed index (default name: metrics) on the indexer:

      [metrics]
      datatype = metric

    Forwarders only need that index to exist on the indexer side.
  * No network egress, no root requirement beyond the Splunk service account.
    Fully standalone add-on with no dependencies.

Install
-------
Install on each monitored host (Apps > Install app from file, splunk install
app, or deployment server), restart Splunk, then verify:

  index=main sourcetype="backup:status" | head

Search quick reference
----------------------
  index=main sourcetype="backup:status" | head
  | mcatalog values(metric_name) where index=metrics metric_name="backup.*" by host
  | mstats avg("backup.*") where index=metrics span=60s by host

Usage
-----
Events: index=main sourcetype=backup:status  (per-backend JSON: configured, snapshots, last age)
Metrics: backup.<backend>_snapshots, backup.<backend>_last_age_hours, backup.timers_active
Configure repositories in local/backup.conf, then restart Splunk.
Dashboards: TA-Backup > Backup Overview / Backup Metrics

Configure
---------
Override the interval or destination index in etc/apps/TA-backup/local/inputs.conf
(never edit default/).

Troubleshooting
---------------
  * restic/borg require the password available to splunkd (env file in local/ or system environment).
  * A host with no backup configured is normal and reports status 'none' - not an alarm.

